## Conv 1 — Stop Button

**Role:** builder
**Skill:** ui-ux-pro-max (phase 1.1 only)
**Stories:** S-01, S-02, S-03

### Verify before edit

Read `HQ/ChatInput/ChatInput.tsx` and `HQ/useHQ.tsx` before touching either. Confirm the exact line ranges for the Send button and `handleSend` in the live files — line numbers may have shifted since the plan was written.

### Phase 1.1 — Design (ui-ux-pro-max)

Produce a written spec for the Stop button before writing any code:

| Attribute | Requirement |
|---|---|
| Icon | Lucide `<Square>` size-13, same container as `<Send>` |
| Color | Muted or destructive accent from existing dark-theme palette — no new colors |
| Position | In-place replacement of Send — no layout shift |
| Enabled | Always clickable when `isLoading === true` |
| Disabled | Normal Send disabled logic when `isLoading === false` |

Get the spec approved (or self-approve as builder) before proceeding.

### Phase 1.2 — ChatInput component

**File:** `studio/src/renderer/src/components/HQ/ChatInput/ChatInput.tsx`

Add to props interface:
```typescript
isLoading?: boolean
onStop?: () => void
```

Button rendering:
- `isLoading === true` → render `<Square size={13} />`, always enabled, `onClick` calls `onStop?.()`
- `isLoading === false` → existing `<Send>` render and disabled logic, unchanged

Enter key guard — in the textarea `onKeyDown` handler:
- If `isLoading === true`: prevent default and return without calling `onSend`

**Done when:** component compiles; `<Square>` renders when `isLoading=true`; Enter blocked during loading.

### Phase 1.3 — Wire stop into useHQ and index

**Files:**
- `studio/src/renderer/src/components/HQ/useHQ.tsx` — add `handleStop`
- `studio/src/renderer/src/components/HQ/index.tsx` — pass `onStop` to `<ChatInput>`

Add `handleStop` in `useHQ.tsx`:
```typescript
function handleStop() {
  abortLlm()
  updateLastMessage({ status: 'done' })
  setLoading(false)
}
```

Pass props in `index.tsx`:
```tsx
<ChatInput
  ...
  isLoading={isLoading}
  onStop={handleStop}
/>
```

`abortLlm` already exists in `llmBridge.ts` — import it if not already imported.

**Done when:** `handleStop` wired; `isLoading` from chatStore passed to `ChatInput`; no TypeScript errors.

### Phase 1.4 — Verify

Manually verify each acceptance criterion:

- AC-01a: Start a stream → `<Square>` renders.
- AC-01b: Stop button is not disabled during streaming.
- AC-01c: Press Enter during streaming → `onSend` not called.
- AC-01d: Stream completes → `<Send>` returns.
- AC-02a: Click Stop → `abortLlm` called (add a `console.log` if needed).
- AC-02b: After Stop → `chatStore.isLoading === false`.
- AC-02c: After Stop → last message `status === 'done'`.
- AC-02d: Click Stop after stream ends → no error thrown, state unchanged.
- AC-02e: Click Stop before first token → message resolves to `done`, content may be empty.
- AC-03a–03c: Partial text visible in bubble; no `streaming` state left in store.

After all pass, write `pathly/plans/chat-stop-proxy/VERIFY.md`:
```
RESULT: PASS
Conv 1 verified: Stop button transforms Send, aborts stream, preserves partial text, no orphaned streaming state.
```

Update `pathly/plans/chat-stop-proxy/PROGRESS.md` — mark all Conv 1 items complete.

